diff --git a/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2611.section.md b/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2611.section.md
index ba0ca25248..454487e1de 100644
--- a/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2611.section.md
+++ b/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes/rl-2611.section.md
@@ -229,6 +229,49 @@ ## Backward Incompatibilities {#sec-release-26.11-incompatibilities}
   Deployments running the server and worker in the same network namespace must also set at least the worker
   `AUTHENTIK_LISTEN__HTTP` address so that the server and worker do not bind to the same address.
 
+- `podman` has been updated to Podman 6.
+  - BoltDB support was dropped. Podman has been automatically migrating to SQLite since 5.8.0 on system reboots.
+  - `iptables` support was dropped, Podman now unconditionally uses its `nftables` backend.
+    This has the side effect that dns in custom networks no longer work without a corresponding firewall rule.
+    This has been the case before when `networking.nftables.enable` was used.
+    Tools like `podman-compose` are also affected by this.
+
+    To mitigate this, add the following code to your NixOS configuration:
+    ```nix
+    {
+      # Do this for every custom network you created.
+      # Replace "podman1" with the interface name.
+      networking.firewall.interfaces."podman1" = {
+        allowedUDPPorts = [ 53 ];
+        allowedTCPPorts = [ 53 ];
+      };
+    }
+    ```
+    Alternatively a wildcard could also be used instead:
+    ```nix
+    {
+      # iptables firewall needs "podman+", nftables needs "podman*"
+      networking.firewall.interfaces."podman${if config.networking.nftables.enable then "*" else "+"}" = {
+        allowedUDPPorts = [ 53 ];
+        allowedTCPPorts = [ 53 ];
+      };
+    }
+    ```
+  - `netavark` is now the only supported networking backend.
+  - `slirp4netns` is no longer supported for rootless networking, `pasta` is now the default and only available option.
+    Existing containers using `slirp4netns` must be migrated using `podman system migrate`.
+  - Configuration was rewritten and now follows the [UAPI.6 Configuration Files Specification](https://uapi-group.org/specifications/specs/configuration_files_specification/).
+
+    See https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/v6.0.0/contrib/design-docs/config-file-parsing.md.
+
+    Configuration files are now split into common, rootful and rootless versions.
+    `virtualisation.containers` was updated to support the new configuration format.
+
+    Configurations which set `graphroot` or `runroot` must move these from the common configuration to the rootful config
+    because rootless podman reads this configuration now as well.
+  - Upgrading with `nixos-rebuild boot` and rebooting is recommended, to complete the BoltDB migration and drop stale iptables rules.
+  - See upstream release notes: https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/v6.1.2/RELEASE_NOTES.md#600
+
 - `qt.platformTheme` no longer supports the `gtk2` option as GTK 2 had reached end-of-life and will be removed in Nixpkgs.
 
 - `services.paperless` has been updated to paperless-ngx 3.0, a major release; review the [upstream v3 migration guide](https://docs.paperless-ngx.com/migration-v3/) before upgrading.
